{#
_partials/_category_tab_glyphs.html.twig — the inbox category icons.
The Gmail category glyphs, one combined path per category — heroicons,
   the set the rest of the app's inline icons draw from. A map here rather
   than a partial per icon: the five are used nowhere else, and the two tab
   strips are the only readers. Two weights of each: the OUTLINE for resting
   tabs and the SOLID for the one you are on — the filled shape is the
   "you are here", the same statement the underline makes, said where the
   eye lands first.

Shared by the unified inbox's tab strip and the account page's, so the two draw
one set of glyphs rather than two copies that drift. Each macro answers the `d`
attribute of a path and nothing else; the svg around it stays with the strip,
because that is where the tint and the data attributes belong.
#}

